      "writtenOn": "2023-12-01T12:08:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Inspecting the code, you don\u0027t actually need `mhandlerThread` being a member field of RoutingCoordinatorService class. Instead, you need a `Looper` for RoutingCoordinatorService. So please make below changes:\n1. Define `Looper mLooper;` as a member field of `RoutingCoordinatorService`\n2. Move `mHandlerThread` to `Dependencies` class and starts it in the Dependencies\u0027s constructor\n3. Define a `RoutingCoordinatorService#getLooper()` for initializing mLooper of RoutingCoordinatorService\n\nThis way, you can use a [TestLooper](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/tests/utils/testutils/java/android/os/test/TestLooper.java) for RoutingCoordinatorService in unit tests. TestLooper allows you to drive the execution of the tasks explicitly (e.g. with `TestLooper#dispatchAll` and `TestLooper#moveTimeForward`), so that you don\u0027t need to wait for a guessed timeout value which is brittle.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 157,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 157,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "67c0ce1cedf3921059fed8a466569917f5f52f31",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
